From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] fix: restamp slice and podset annotations when reapplying ray manifests to prevent worker gating

Re-applying declarative manifests for running elastic RayClusters strips workload slice annotations and podset labels that were stamped at start time by the reconciler, leaving newly created workers permanently gated.

Kueue's RayCluster defaulting webhook stamps the kueue.x-k8s.io/podset label, workload slice annotations, and scheduling gates only during CREATE operations. When external configuration management tools re-apply the original RayCluster manifest, the webhook does not intercept the UPDATE, resulting in unstamped pod templates that fail Kueue scheduling gate validation.

Register the RayCluster mutating webhook for UPDATE operations and re-stamp required slice annotations, podset labels, queue labels, scheduling gates, and flavor placement on each modification. Preserve existing slice assignments and first-slice workload annotations so template re-stamping operates idempotently across repeated manifest applications.
---
